---
source: crates/agentgateway/src/import/litellm.rs
description: src/tests/import/litellm/db-state-ambiguous-mcp-grant.yaml
---
source: litellm
config:
  config:
    database:
      url: "sqlite://data.db"
  gateways:
    default:
      port: 4000
  ui:
    gateways: default
  llm:
    gateways: default
    models:
      - name: chat
        provider: openAI
        params:
          model: gpt-4o
    policies:
      apiKey:
        keys:
          - key: $LITELLM_MASTER_KEY
            metadata:
              name: master
          - keyHash: "sha256:aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111aaaa1111"
            metadata:
              name: intern
        mode: strict
findings:
  - sourcePath: "model_list[0]"
    status: exact
    message: Imported model deployment for chat
  - sourcePath: general_settings.master_key
    status: approximate
    message: "Mapped LiteLLM's master_key (an admin-equivalent credential, not a per-user virtual key) to strict Authorization Bearer authentication; LiteLLM also accepts other credential headers. Per-user virtual-key migration needs LiteLLM's database state, not config.yaml alone."
  - sourcePath: mcp_servers.hr_payroll
    status: approximate
    message: "Renamed \"hr_payroll\" to \"hr-payroll\" to satisfy agentgateway's Gateway-API-style MCP target name pattern (lowercase letters, digits, '-', '.'; no underscores)"
  - sourcePath: mcp_servers.hr_payroll
    status: unsupported
    message: "This server is restricted to specific virtual keys via DB-managed object_permission.mcp_servers grants, which config.yaml alone cannot express; it was not emitted rather than exposing it to every caller"
  - sourcePath: mcp_servers.hr-payroll
    status: unsupported
    message: "This server is restricted to specific virtual keys via DB-managed object_permission.mcp_servers grants, which config.yaml alone cannot express; it was not emitted rather than exposing it to every caller"
  - sourcePath: "db_state.keys[0]"
    status: exact
    message: "Migrated key \"intern\" to llm.policies.apiKey (hash-based, no plaintext)"
  - sourcePath: db_state.mcp_servers.hr-payroll
    status: unsupported
    message: "MCP target name \"hr-payroll\" is shared by more than one held-back LiteLLM server; a grant can't be resolved to the right one, so none of them were migrated"
  - sourcePath: db_state.mcp_servers.hr-payroll
    status: unsupported
    message: "MCP target name \"hr-payroll\" is shared by more than one held-back LiteLLM server; a grant can't be resolved to the right one, so none of them were migrated"
